(A library is not a warehouse of finished thoughts but an instrument for producing new ones. The) Tj T*
(shelf is the argument: what stands beside what, which spine catches the eye on the way to) Tj T*
(somewhere else, which book has been pulled so often that it no longer sits flush with its) Tj T*
(neighbours. Cataloguing systems try to freeze this into an order, and every reader quietly) Tj T*
